From: Petr Wozniak <petr.wozniak@gmail.com>
Subject: [PATCH] map-agent 989: a link of an AP-MLD does not get a BSS of its own

uci_apply_wps_credentials() is the only place in map-agent that creates a
wireless section, and it creates one for every AP it applies M2 credentials
to. On a node whose fronthaul and backhaul are AP-MLDs that is wrong twice
over: the network is already on the air as a link of the MLD, and the extra
BSS takes a slot the MLD needs for an affiliated AP.

Two symptoms that cost a full day each turned out to be this one line.

1. Legacy per-radio BSSes came back on the controller after every clean
   flash, although map_genconfig had been fixed to stop generating them.
   The producer is identifiable from the order of the options it writes:

     map_genconfig:  device, ifname, mode, disabled, ...
     map-agent:      ifname, ieee80211k, bss_transition, ...

   The sections that reappeared had the second fingerprint. The genconfig
   fix worked; it was simply not the producer.

2. The bhmld placeholders - mapagent 'ap' sections that exist so that
   apmld_parse() runs for the backhaul MLD, and that name interfaces which
   are not meant to exist as netdevs - materialised as real, transmitting
   BSSes on some nodes and not others:

     4g   0 bhmld BSSes      8g   1        x8   2

   Not a property of the node. wifi_get_first_available_ifname() hands the
   credentials to the first torn-down 'ap' section on the radio, so whether
   a placeholder is picked depends on whether a legacy backhaul section on
   that radio absorbed the M2 first. 4g still had legacy sections on both
   radios, 8g on one, x8 on neither - which is exactly 0, 1 and 2. The
   fault looked like it wandered between nodes because the outcome depends
   on config order, not on the node.

   Note the coupling: removing the legacy sections (1) frees the slot, so
   the placeholders would then be picked on every node. The two fixes only
   make sense together.

Keep writing the mapagent 'ap' section - the mesh layer needs it for mld_id
and the AP-MLD Config TLV, and it is what carries the credentials into the
AP-MLD - and skip only the wireless section. This is the same split, and the
same reasoning, that map_genconfig already applies on its side.

The fronthaul asks the wireless config whether an AP-MLD already serves this
SSID on this radio, not the mapagent MLD list. Measured 2026-07-29 with an
earlier version of this patch that asked the mapagent list: on a boot where
map_genconfig had left mapagent without a single 'mld' section, the lookup
found nothing and both per-radio fronthaul BSSes went back on the air. The
wireless section is what hostapd runs, so it is there for as long as the MLD
is, which is exactly the condition being asked about.

Verified on hardware 2026-07-28 in the state this patch reproduces from a
clean flash: three nodes, ap-mld-1 and ap-mld-2 and nothing else on the air,
all six MLDs reporting non-zero num_ap, both backhauls two-legged, and the
state still holding after ten hours untouched.

Signed-off-by: Petr Wozniak <petr.wozniak@gmail.com>
---
diff -urN a/src/config.c b/src/config.c
--- a/src/config.c	2026-07-29 07:18:27.328430523 +0200
+++ b/src/config.c	2026-07-29 07:18:27.330189931 +0200
@@ -924,6 +924,89 @@
 }
 
 /* TODO: batch the changes arther than commit oneby one */
+/* Is this network already on the air as a link of an AP-MLD?
+ *
+ * In the single-netdev MLO model the AP-MLD has one wireless section spanning
+ * every participating radio (ap-mld-1 with a device list), and its affiliated
+ * APs have no wireless section of their own. A per-radio BSS created here
+ * would advertise the same network a second time and, worse, take a BSS slot
+ * the MLD needs for an affiliated AP.
+ *
+ * Measured on hardware 2026-07-28: the node that came up with four such BSSes
+ * reported num_ap=0 for both its MLDs, while nodes with one reported 2 and 3.
+ * Deleting them by hand and rebooting brought all three nodes to non-zero
+ * num_ap for the first time that day. Which node got the most varied from boot
+ * to boot, so the defect looked like it moved between nodes.
+ *
+ * Ask the wireless config, not the mapagent MLD list. The wireless section is
+ * what hostapd actually runs, so it is present for as long as the MLD is on
+ * the air; the mapagent 'mld' sections are written by map_genconfig and can be
+ * absent exactly when the credentials arrive. Measured 2026-07-29: a boot that
+ * left mapagent without a single mld section put both per-radio fronthaul
+ * BSSes back on the air, because the lookup had nothing to find.
+ *
+ * The backhaul asks neither - it asks mapagent.agent.mld_backhaul, the switch
+ * map_genconfig already uses for this same decision. That also covers a band
+ * the backhaul MLD does not span (2.4 GHz), where a per-radio backhaul BSS is
+ * not a duplicate but is unwanted all the same: two backhauls bridged into
+ * br-lan are an L2 loop, measured at 56k pkt/s on 2026-07-28.
+ *
+ * Opt-in either way: a mesh without an MLD backhaul, or with no AP-MLD serving
+ * this SSID on this radio, is unaffected.
+ */
+static bool wireless_ap_mld_covers(struct uci_context *ctx,
+				   struct uci_package *pkg,
+				   const char *ssid, const char *device)
+{
+	struct uci_element *e;
+
+	uci_foreach_element(&pkg->sections, e) {
+		struct uci_section *s = uci_to_section(e);
+		struct uci_element *d;
+		struct uci_option *o;
+		const char *val;
+
+		if (strcmp(s->type, UCI_WLAN_IFACE))
+			continue;
+
+		val = uci_lookup_option_string(ctx, s, "mlo");
+		if (!val || atoi(val) != 1)
+			continue;
+
+		val = uci_lookup_option_string(ctx, s, "ssid");
+		if (!val || strcmp(val, ssid))
+			continue;
+
+		o = uci_lookup_option(ctx, s, "device");
+		if (!o)
+			continue;
+
+		if (o->type == UCI_TYPE_STRING)
+			return !strcmp(o->v.string, device);
+
+		uci_foreach_element(&o->v.list, d) {
+			if (!strcmp(d->name, device))
+				return true;
+		}
+	}
+
+	return false;
+}
+
+static bool mld_serves_network(struct agent_config *cfg, struct uci_context *ctx,
+			       struct uci_package *pkg, char *ssid,
+			       char *device, uint8_t multi_ap)
+{
+#if (EASYMESH_VERSION >= 6)
+	if (multi_ap == 0x01)
+		return cfg->mld_backhaul;
+
+	return wireless_ap_mld_covers(ctx, pkg, ssid, device);
+#else
+	return false;
+#endif
+}
+
 struct netif_apcfg *uci_apply_wps_credentials(struct agent_config *cfg, char *ifname,
 				 char *device, struct wps_credential *out,
 				 struct wsc_ext *exts)
@@ -1092,6 +1175,19 @@
 		char section_name[32] = {0};
 		char *psep;
 
+		/* The mapagent 'ap' section written above stays: the mesh layer
+		 * needs it for mld_id and the AP-MLD Config TLV. Only the
+		 * wireless section - the thing that would actually go on the air
+		 * as a BSS of its own - is skipped.
+		 */
+		if (mld_serves_network(cfg, ctx, pkg, ssid, device, multi_ap)) {
+			agnt_dbg(LOG_APCFG, "%s: %s is a link of an AP-MLD, "
+				 "no BSS of its own\n", __func__, ifname);
+			uci_unload(ctx, pkg);
+			uci_free_context(ctx);
+			return ap;
+		}
+
 		snprintf(section_name, sizeof(section_name),
 				 "%s_ap", ifname);
 
@@ -2321,6 +2417,7 @@
 		A_MLD_AP_PREFIX,
 		A_MLD_STA_PREFIX,
 		A_PHYSICAL_MLD,
+		A_MLD_BACKHAUL,
 #endif
 		A_ASSOC_CTRL_FILE,
 		NUM_POLICIES
@@ -2365,6 +2462,7 @@
 		[A_MLD_AP_PREFIX] = { .name = "mld_ap_prefix", .type = UCI_TYPE_STRING },
 		[A_MLD_STA_PREFIX] = { .name = "mld_sta_prefix", .type = UCI_TYPE_STRING },
 		[A_PHYSICAL_MLD] = { .name = "physical_mld", .type = UCI_TYPE_STRING },
+		[A_MLD_BACKHAUL] = { .name = "mld_backhaul", .type = UCI_TYPE_STRING },
 #endif
 		[A_ASSOC_CTRL_FILE] = { .name = "assoc_ctrl_file", .type = UCI_TYPE_STRING },
 	};
@@ -2542,6 +2640,11 @@
 		a->physical_mld = !!atoi(tb[A_PHYSICAL_MLD]->v.string);
 	else
 		a->physical_mld = true;
+
+	if (tb[A_MLD_BACKHAUL])
+		a->mld_backhaul = !!atoi(tb[A_MLD_BACKHAUL]->v.string);
+	else
+		a->mld_backhaul = false;
 #endif
 
 	if (tb[A_ASSOC_CTRL_FILE]) {
diff -urN a/src/config.h b/src/config.h
--- a/src/config.h	2026-07-29 07:18:27.328704704 +0200
+++ b/src/config.h	2026-07-29 07:18:27.328833942 +0200
@@ -316,6 +316,7 @@
 	char mld_ap_prefix[IFNAMSIZ - 1]; /* AP prefix + %1d */
 	char mld_sta_prefix[IFNAMSIZ - 1]; /* STA prefix + %1d */
 	bool physical_mld;
+	bool mld_backhaul;   /* backhaul is an AP-MLD, not per-radio BSSes */
 #endif
 	atimer_t metric_report_timer;
 };
